
export anchor FixTestFailures:
    userPrompt:
        \\\
        Failure during testing failures:

        ---- main_window::tests::reset_brightness_sits_beneath_the_slider stdout ----

        thread 'main_window::tests::reset_brightness_sits_beneath_the_slider' (16434) panicked at src/main_window.rs:2376:13:
        resetting changed the mode
        note: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace

        ---- main_window::tests::the_brightness_slider_brightens_the_interface stdout ----

        thread 'main_window::tests::the_brightness_slider_brightens_the_interface' (16468) panicked at src/main_window.rs:2470:9:
        assertion `left == right` failed: the thumb isn't on dark mode at 0
          left: Some(157.0)
         right: Some(17.0)

        ---- prompt_mode::tests::long_output_is_measured_a_few_rows_a_frame stdout ----

        thread 'prompt_mode::tests::long_output_is_measured_a_few_rows_a_frame' (17078) panicked at src/prompt_mode.rs:15610:9:
        3965 of 1500 rows were drawn in the first frame


        failures:
            main_window::tests::reset_brightness_sits_beneath_the_slider
            main_window::tests::the_brightness_slider_brightens_the_interface
            prompt_mode::tests::long_output_is_measured_a_few_rows_a_frame

        test result: FAILED. 495 passed; 3 failed; 1 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 52.67s

        error: test failed, to rerun pass `--bin suspense`
        Error: Process completed with exit code 101.
        \\\

    mode: code

    newConversation: false

    systemPrompt:
        \\\
        We're working on the code, located in ./src. Change the code so it does what the prompt asks, as the spec describes it.

        The spec's Piton source is in ./spec. Don't change it, and don't read it to learn what the spec says: read the compiled reference instead, as above. If the prompt asks for something the spec doesn't describe, or describes differently, say so in your reply rather than working around it.

        Before changing anything, write the constraints this task must meet to ${UNDERSTANDING_FILE}, and keep it current as you read more of the spec. It is a Markdown list and nothing else: one line per constraint, at most twelve, each a single short, specific statement of what must be true, written as a link to the compiled reference file it comes from, such as `- [The chain tab has no bottom border in combined mode](.claude/reference/scope/prompt-mode/chat-input/index.md#chain)`. Only list what the spec says; leave out anything you are deciding yourself. Replace a constraint when you learn it was wrong rather than adding another.
        \\\
